WEBVTT

00:00:57.496 --> 00:01:00.621
that controls your body’s 
response to stress.

00:01:01.537 --> 00:01:03.954
When your brain detects
a stressful situation

00:01:03.996 --> 00:01:07.079
your HPA axis is instantly activated

00:01:07.121 --> 00:01:12.413
and releases a hormone called “cortisol”
that set your body for immediate action.

00:01:13.163 --> 00:01:16.329
Yet, high levels of cortisol
over long periods of time

00:01:16.371 --> 00:01:18.538
wreak havoc in your brain.

00:01:18.704 --> 00:01:22.079
For example, chronic stress
increases the activity level

00:01:22.121 --> 00:01:25.121
and the number of nerve connections
in the amygdala,

00:01:25.163 --> 00:01:27.829
your brain’s warning system.

00:01:28.413 --> 00:01:30.538
And when the cortisol levels increase,